  "description": "51 Mayola Road",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;All new external facing and roofing materials in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works carried out in this connection) shall match those of the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance including type, size, colour, bond, pointing, coursing, jointing, profile and texture (delete as appropriate)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\nREASON: In order to preserve the character and appearance of the host building and surrounding area.\r\n&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development must be carried out in accordance with the approved details, including the detailed specifications, drainage layout, and management and maintenance plan submitted under reference 2025/0270. The approved scheme for a sustainable drainage system - which includes an infiltration test for any soakaways - must ensure no increase in surface water discharge off-site and an overall reduction in peak flow rate and volume.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure the development is carried out in line with the approved details for flood risk mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the original permission ref&amp;nbsp;2024/2641 dated&amp;nbsp;24/01/2025.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
